    "knowledge_point": "Applying De Moivre's Theorem",
    "problem": "Simplify the expression ${[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})]}^{20}.$",
    "worked_solution": "De Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=20$ and $\\phi =\\frac{2\\theta }{5}.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\theta }{5})]}^{20} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\cdot \\frac{2\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\cdot \\frac{2\\theta }{5}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
